@title Wiring guide: three steps in words on the canvas, rings on free pins
@area Schematic
@sizes 1366x768 1920x1080
# The wire tool says where you are (start, turn, finish) at the bottom of the drawing, marks the current step with
# an arrow, says how many pins are free (ringed), and rings every pin that can still take a wire. The guide is
# deliberate: a quiet strip over the drawing that is only there while the wire tool is on (Esc removes it).
click_text "New project"
wait 20
key q
text mcb
key Return
click 600 150
wait 10
key q
text contactor
key Return
click 600 300
wait 10
key Escape
key w
wait 3
move 800 450
wait 3
shot step-1-start
expect_scene "wire"
click 800 450
wait 3
shot refused-start-not-doubled
key Escape
key w
wait 3
click 596 160
move 700 420
wait 3
shot step-2-turn
move 596 338
wait 3
shot step-3-finish-on-a-pin
key Escape
wait 3
shot guide-gone-after-escape
